' 15 Normalization of the Reified syntax: from source text to the bytes of a Par.
'
' Source of Figure 1 in ../syntax-contract.md. The figure restates
' Compiler::source_to_adt (rholang/src/rust/interpreter/compiler/compiler.rs),
' the dispatch of normalize_ann_proc (compiler/normalize.rs), the P3b arms
' (compiler/normalizer/processes/) and the P2 builders
' (models/src/rust/reified/builders.rs). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. The baseline float rewrite runs first, and the v3 parser reads the text.
'      The external scanner decides whether `use` and `free` are keywords.
'   2. The parser rejects a malformed params section or query by variant.
'   3. The dispatch sends each Reified AST part to its arm. An arm normalizes
'      the parts in the scope of the syntax contract and calls one builder.
'   4. The builders and the validators re-check every parser guarantee.
'   5. The sorter puts the marker tuples in canonical order, and prost gives
'      the bytes that the dual-frontend corpus pins.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 15-syntax-normalization.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 15-syntax-normalization
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam PartitionBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title Normalization of the Reified syntax: Compiler::source_to_adt

start
:source text; <<$rrs_host>>
:preprocess_floats: the baseline rewrite of unsuffixed floats to f64
(retired at the final parser pin); <<$rrs_host>>
partition "v3 parser (tree-sitter grammar, external scanner, AST builder)" {
  :the scanner reads `use` and `free`:
  a keyword only when the next text can never continue a baseline program,
  an ordinary identifier otherwise; <<$rrs_syntax>>
  :the AST builder walks each params section and each query once; <<$rrs_syntax>>
  if (a repeated key, a positional param after a named one,
a key that is not an identifier, or a malformed query?) then (yes)
    :ParserError "Parse failed: <variant> at <span>"
    no Par; <<$rrs_reject>>
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
}
:AST with UseBlock, NameDecl.space, FreeTheory,
Hyperparam lists and QuerySpec; <<$rrs_syntax>>
partition "Normalizer arms (one adapter for each Reified AST part)" {
  split
    :UseBlock
    normalize_p_use_block:
    space and body in the current scope; <<$rrs_syntax>>
    :use_block; <<$rrs_syntax>>
  split again
    :New with annotations
    normalize_p_new:
    annotations in the scope outside the new,
    in binding order; <<$rrs_syntax>>
    :new_space; <<$rrs_syntax>>
  split again
    :FreeTheory
    normalize_p_free_theory:
    arguments in the current scope; <<$rrs_syntax>>
    :efree; <<$rrs_syntax>>
  split again
    :Send params (also the !? and !m desugarings)
    normalize_p_send:
    values after the data, in the current scope; <<$rrs_syntax>>
    :send_params; <<$rrs_syntax>>
  split again
    :Receive query
    normalize_p_input:
    channel, payload, then params,
    in the scope outside the receive; <<$rrs_syntax>>
    :query_spec; <<$rrs_syntax>>
  end split
}
if (a builder or a validator rejects the parts?) then (yes)
  :NormalizerError "reified syntax: <message>"
  no Par; <<$rrs_reject>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
:marker tuples in their recognized positions:
USE and NEWSPACE in Par.exprs, PARAMS as the last data element,
QUERY as the bind source, FREE as a value; <<$rrs_syntax>>
:ParSortMatcher sorts the Par: the marker tuples need no new sort score; <<$rrs_host>>
:prost bytes of the Par, pinned by test-vectors/reified-syntax-corpus-v1.json; <<$rrs_host>>
stop

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_syntax>     | Reified syntax: parser, normalizer arms, builders, marker tuples |
|<$rrs_host>       | baseline code that the campaign does not change |
|<$rrs_reject>     | rejection: the source gives no Par |
endlegend
@enduml
